        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing, and one answer has to be chosen. Choose the answer the documents support better.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Port Vincent?\n\nAnswer A: 741\n  about: Port Vincent, Louisiana\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: United States Census Bureau\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The population was 741 at the 2010 census.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: 741\n  about: Port Vincent\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"Its population at the 2010 census was 741 and a population density of 423\"\" [document 3]\n\nAnswer C: 1,234\n  about: Port Vincent\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2010\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"The population was 1,234 at the 2010 census.\" [document 4]\n\nAnswer D: 472\n  about: Port Vincent\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"At the , Port Vincent had a population of 472.\" [document 5]\n\nThe documents:\nDocument 1: Port Vincent, Louisiana Port Vincent is a village in Livingston Parish, Louisiana, United States. The population was 741 at the 2010 census. It is part of the Baton Rouge Metropolitan Statistical Area. Port Vincent is located at (30.337250, -90.841927). According to the United States Census Bureau, the village has a total area of 1.7 square miles (4.4 km²), of which 1.6 square miles (4.3 km²) is land and 0.04 square mile (0.1 km²) (2.37%) is water. As of the census of 2000, there were 463 people, 192 households, and 134 families residing in the village. The population density was 280.3\nDocument 3: Port Vincent , LA - Geographic Facts & Maps - MapSof.net MapSof.net Places Countries States Capital Cities Cities Static Maps Physical Political Topo Relief Historical Satellite Road Street Climate Map Tools Distance Calculator Address Locator Street View Geocoder Tool Coordinates Search North America United States Louisiana Livingston Parish Port Vincent Port Vincent , Louisiana Port Vincent : Human settlement in Louisiana , United States of America About Port Vincent is a city located in the county of Livingston Parish in the U.S. state of Louisiana . Its population at the 2010 census was 741 and a population density of 423\nDocument 4: Elevation 7 ft ( 2 m ) Population ( 2020 ) • Total 1,234 • Density 379.11/sq mi ( 146.41/km 2 ) Time zone UTC-6 ( CST ) • Summer ( DST ) UTC-5 ( CDT ) Area code 225 FIPS code 22-62105 Website portvincent-la.gov Port Vincent is a village in Livingston Parish, Louisiana, United States. The population was 1,234 at the 2010 census. It is part of the Baton Rouge Metropolitan Statistical Area. Geography [ edit ] Port Vincent is located at 30°20′14″N 90°50′31″W ﻿ / ﻿ 30.33722°N 90.84194°W ﻿ / 30.33722 ;\nDocument 5: Port Vincent, South Australia Port Vincent is a small town on the east coast of Yorke Peninsula in South Australia, 194 km from Adelaide by road. At the , Port Vincent had a population of 472. The Narungga Aborigines inhabited the area prior to white settlement. The town was laid out by Adelaide solicitor L.M. Cullen in 1877, originally known as Surveyor's Point. In its early days it was a port exporting wheat, barley, wool and mallee stumps (firewood). From the first settlement in 1852 until 1877, coastal trading ketches would beach at high tide, and unload directly to farm\n\nWeigh the evidence. Which documents are specific, and consistent within themselves: do their names, dates and other details fit together? Which fit what the other documents say? Does any document read as altered, or out of place? Judge by the documents alone.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"reason\": \"one or two sentences\", \"choice\": \"A\"}"
